From 47219011ff8308124c904aee605d97e189bf808b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:36:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: great people, residents, deeds, golden ages and an AI
 rule that spends them

Implements notes/freeciv45/design/great-people.md on the civ45 ruleset:

- Seven great-person unit types (Great Sage, Builder, Magnate, Virtuoso,
  Oracle, Commander, Spymaster) with the user flag GreatPerson: cost 240,
  pop_cost 1, strength 0, NonMil, NoVeteran, NoBuild, Unbribable, AddToCity;
  the Builder has HelpWonder, the Spymaster Diplomat. Art borrowed until the
  tileset draws u.great_*.
- Great-person points as User_Effect_3 rows per building (1 to 3 for city
  improvements by tier, 2 per wonder and per Resident), User_Effect_4 as the
  golden age multiplier; seven Resident buildings, the Sanctum and the Golden
  Age small wonder with their effects (buildings nobody can build: MinYear
  9999).
- actions.ruleset: User Action 3 (Great Deed) and User Action 4 (Pledge a
  Golden Age), both self-targeted and consuming; deed enablers for a Sage,
  Virtuoso or Oracle in a city of their own, the Magnate in any city and the
  Commander anywhere; one Join City enabler per kind that needs no Resident
  of that kind in the city, the stock one excluding great people; great
  people kept out of Disband Unit Recover.
- script.lua: pools per city (150 + 75 per birth), births drawn by the
  city's sources, a free great person for the first to Philosophy, Theology,
  Economics or Electricity, the Resident on Join City, the deeds (a tech,
  gold, 400 history, the Sanctum, a veteran level for the stack), pledges
  and the timed golden age, and a turn_begin rule that spends every AI
  great person through the same actions. Counters are scalar globals named
  by integer ids so the saved script state loads back.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45      |  16 ++
 data/civ45/actions.ruleset   | 153 ++++++++++
 data/civ45/buildings.ruleset | 207 ++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/effects.ruleset   | 533 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/script.lua        | 308 ++++++++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/units.ruleset     | 267 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1484 insertions(+)

diff --git a/data/civ45/README.civ45 b/data/civ45/README.civ45
index fd3a33c..adfafdc 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -94,6 +94,22 @@ Differences from sandbox
   AEGIS Cruiser Missile Cruiser, SSBN Missile Submarine, ICBM Nuclear
   Missile), so saves and scripts load. Jaguar Warrior, Immortal, Alpine
   Troops, Crusaders and Mechanic are gone (Engineers heal vehicles).
+- Great people (notes/freeciv45/design/great-people.md): every city
+  collects great-person points from its temples, libraries, markets,
+  theatres, courts and their successors (1 to 3 a turn), from wonders
+  and settled great people (2); at 150 points, plus 75 for every great
+  person the player had before, one of seven kinds is born (Great Sage,
+  Builder, Magnate, Virtuoso, Oracle, Commander, Spymaster), drawn by the
+  city's sources. Each settles (Join City founds a Resident building:
+  +25% science, +3 shields, +3 trade and +25% gold, +3 history and +25%
+  luxury, two content, Veteran_Build, spy resistance), does a deed once
+  (a free tech, 240 shields into a wonder, a trade mission, 400 history,
+  the Sanctum, a veteran level for the stack, or the diplomat actions)
+  or pledges a golden age: ten turns of +1 shield and +1 trade on
+  working tiles, double points and no anarchy, for one pledge, then two,
+  then three. The first to Philosophy, Theology, Economics or
+  Electricity gets one free. script.lua runs it, and spends the AI's
+  great people for it each turn through the same actions.
 - Strategic resources: Swordsmen, Macebearers, Crossbowmen, Knights,
   Cannon, Ship of the Line and Ironclad need Iron (Ironclad Coal too),
   War Elephants Ivory, and armour, aircraft and modern warships Oil,
